# function helper(o) { o() }  function kept() {}  function run(callee, operand) { if (callee is helper) { .. } else callee(operand) }  run(helper, kept)
# The front end writes a call of a helper out behind `IsClosureOf` and leaves the call itself on the other side. What arrives there is anything but a closure of the helper, whatever the type
# of the tested value says: where the helper alone can arrive, nothing is called, and the operands go nowhere.
